    "lawCode": "Add Title 26 Chap 13 §26-1301, NYC Ad Cd",
    "lawSection": "New York City Administrative Code",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1789A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the administrative code of the city of New York, in\nrelation to certification of payment of rent by the human resources\nadministration to the tenant\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nRequires the Human Resources Administration, whenever rent is paid to\na landlord on behalf of a tenant receiving public assistance, to make\navailable through an online client portal, a certification of payment.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nAmends title twenty-six of the Administrative Code of the City of New\nYork by adding a new chapter thirteen.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis bill provides tenants on public assistance the right to obtain\nproof of rental payment made by the New York City Human Resources\nAdministration (HRA). This legislation is deemed necessary because\nthere are hundreds of cases whereby tenants whose rent is paid by HRA\nare summoned to landlord/tenant court for non-payment of rent. For\nmany, this legislation could prevent such disputes from being elevated\nto the court level. Tenants on public assistance are rarely aware of\nthe fact that HRA has paid the landlord. Such confirmation, through an\nonline client portal, provides the tenant with proof of payment when\ncalled into court.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2016: S154 - REFERRED TO CITIES/ advanced to third reading\n2015: S154 - COMMITTED TO RULES/ referred to cities\n2013-2014: S206/A2658 - REFERRED TO CITIES/advanced to third reading\n2011-2012: S24/A619 - REFERRED TO CITIES/advanced to third reading\n2010: S5992/A1439-A - PASSED SENATE/Passed Assembly\n2007: A.619\n2005-2006: A.735\n2003-2004: A.5510\n2001-2002: A.6545-A\n1999-2000: A.1518/S.2111\n1997-1998: A.5675\n1995-1996: A.5578/S.3252\n1993-1994: A.6269/S.3881\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred twentieth day after it\nshall have become law.\n",
